---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import StaticPage from '../layouts/StaticPage.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { slugify } from '../utils/slug';
import '../styles/about.css';

// Topics that already have published guides get a live link; the rest show "coming soon".
const posts = await getCollection('blog');
const liveTopics = new Set(posts.map((p) => p.data.topic).filter(Boolean));

const topicList = [
	{ name: 'Airline Baggage Fees & Carry-On Rules', icon: 'plane', c1: '#0a3d62', c2: '#2380c4', blurb: 'Size limits, weight caps and extra fees, airline by airline.' },
	{ name: 'TSA, Security & Venue Bag Rules', icon: 'shield', c1: '#1b2447', c2: '#4c5fb0', blurb: 'What clears security at airports, stadiums and venues.' },
	{ name: 'Luggage, Suitcases & Brands', icon: 'luggage', c1: '#0b5f59', c2: '#1fb5a6', blurb: 'Hardside, softside and carry-on picks compared.' },
	{ name: 'Backpacks', icon: 'backpack', c1: '#9a4a07', c2: '#f0a02a', blurb: 'Daypacks, travel packs and commuter bags.' },
	{ name: 'Hiking, Camping & Outdoor Gear', icon: 'mountain', c1: '#12482a', c2: '#47a05f', blurb: 'Trail-ready packs and outdoor carry gear.' },
	{ name: 'Handbags, Totes & Designer Bags', icon: 'bag', c1: '#8a1546', c2: '#e5568a', blurb: 'Totes, crossbodies and designer bags worth carrying.' },
	{ name: 'Specialty, Sports, Kids & Duffel Bags', icon: 'duffel', c1: '#4a1d96', c2: '#8b5cf6', blurb: 'Duffels, sports bags and kids’ travel bags.' },
	{ name: 'Packing & Travel Accessories', icon: 'package', c1: '#a53a0a', c2: '#f98a45', blurb: 'Packing cubes, locks, tags and organizers that earn their space.' },
	{ name: 'Luggage & Bag Care, Repair & Services', icon: 'wrench', c1: '#2b3a4d', c2: '#6b8099', blurb: 'Cleaning, repairs and replacement parts that extend a bag’s life.' },
].map((t) => ({
	...t,
	style: `--c1:${t.c1};--c2:${t.c2}`,
	href: liveTopics.has(t.name) ? `/topic/${slugify(t.name)}/` : undefined,
	soon: !liveTopics.has(t.name),
}));

const personLd = JSON.stringify({
	'@context': 'https://schema.org',
	'@type': 'Person',
	name: 'Iver Calloway',
	jobTitle: 'Travel Gear Specialist & Frequent Flyer',
	image: 'https://baggagegear.com/iver-calloway.jpg',
	url: 'https://baggagegear.com/about/',
	homeLocation: { '@type': 'Place', name: 'Miami, Florida, United States' },
	knowsAbout: ['Luggage reviews', 'Airline baggage policy', 'Carry-on optimization', 'Packing strategy', 'One-bag travel'],
	sameAs: ['https://www.facebook.com/IverCalloway/'],
	worksFor: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Baggage Gear', url: 'https://baggagegear.com/' },
});
---

<StaticPage
	title="About Baggage Gear"
	description="Meet Iver Calloway, a former airline ground operations supervisor who tests luggage in real transit. Honest bag reviews, airline baggage rules and packing advice."
	c1="#0f2f45"
	c2="#3b7f8f"
	wide
>
	<div slot="hero" class="ab-hero">
		<div>
			<h1 class="sp-hero-title">Luggage advice from the other side of the check-in counter</h1>
			<p class="sp-hero-lead">
				Baggage Gear is run by Iver Calloway, a former airline ground operations supervisor. Every bag here is
				judged by how it survives real travel, not how it looks on a showroom shelf.
			</p>
			<div class="ab-hero-cta">
				<a class="btn" href="#how-i-test"><Icon name="route" size={18} /> See how I test bags</a>
				<a class="btn ghost" href="/contact/"><Icon name="mail" size={18} /> Contact Iver</a>
			</div>
		</div>
		<aside class="tag" aria-label="Author card for Iver Calloway">
			<span class="tag-strap" aria-hidden="true"></span>
			<div class="tag-body">
				<span class="tag-hole" aria-hidden="true"></span>
				<img class="tag-photo" src="/iver-calloway.jpg" alt="Portrait of Iver Calloway" width="112" height="112" />
				<p class="tag-name">Iver Calloway</p>
				<p class="tag-role">Travel Gear Specialist &amp; Frequent Flyer</p>
				<div class="tag-route"><b>MIA</b><small>Miami, Florida<br />United States</small></div>
				<ul class="tag-stats">
					<li><strong>9</strong><span>years in airline ground ops</span></li>
					<li><strong>60+</strong><span>flight segments a year</span></li>
					<li><strong>250+</strong><span>bags and accessories reviewed</span></li>
				</ul>
				<div class="tag-bars" aria-hidden="true"></div>
			</div>
		</aside>
	</div>

	<script type="application/ld+json" is:inline set:html={personLd}></script>

	<div class="sec-head" style="margin-top:0">
		<span class="chip" style="--c1:#0f2f45;--c2:#3b7f8f"><Icon name="user" /></span>
		<h2>Hi, I’m Iver</h2>
	</div>
	<p class="ab-intro">
		I’m Iver Calloway, and I live in Miami, Florida. I spent nine years as an airline ground operations
		supervisor, and today I fly more than 60 segments a year with a bag I’m trying to break. I write this site
		for the person standing in front of a wall of suitcases, or looking at an airline fee table, and wondering
		what is actually worth buying.
	</p>
	<p>
		This page is not a résumé. It is the short version of who I am, why you can trust what I say, and just as
		important, where my knowledge stops.
	</p>
	<ul class="facts">
		<li><span class="dot" style="--d:#2380c4"></span>Based in Miami, Florida</li>
		<li><span class="dot" style="--d:#0b9c8d"></span>Aviation and plane spotting</li>
		<li><span class="dot" style="--d:#f0a02a"></span>Travel points and miles</li>
		<li><span class="dot" style="--d:#8b5cf6"></span>One-bag travel</li>
		<li><span class="dot" style="--d:#e5568a"></span>Scuba diving</li>
		<li><span class="dot" style="--d:#f98a45"></span>Latin cuisine</li>
	</ul>

	<div class="sec-head">
		<span class="chip" style="--c1:#9a4a07;--c2:#f0a02a"><Icon name="briefcase" /></span>
		<h2>How I ended up in luggage</h2>
	</div>
	<p>
		I learned what luggage can and can’t survive from behind the counter. For nine years I worked in airline
		ground operations, supervising baggage handling and working with airline policy every day. I saw which bags
		came off the belt looking fine and which ones were finished after a single trip: gate checks, tight
		connections, rough conveyor belts.
	</p>
	<p>
		That job left me with an annoying habit. I can’t look at a suitcase without checking the wheels and the zipper
		first. Baggage Gear is where I put that habit to work for you.
	</p>
	<ol class="timeline">
		<li>
			<span class="chip" style="--c1:#0a3d62;--c2:#2380c4"><Icon name="plane" /></span>
			<div>
				<strong>9 years in airline ground operations</strong>
				<p>Supervising baggage handling and applying airline baggage policy at the airport.</p>
			</div>
		</li>
		<li>
			<span class="chip" style="--c1:#9a4a07;--c2:#f0a02a"><Icon name="route" /></span>
			<div>
				<strong>Now flying 60+ segments a year</strong>
				<p>I travel to test luggage in real transit conditions, not in a showroom.</p>
			</div>
		</li>
		<li>
			<span class="chip" style="--c1:#0b5f59;--c2:#1fb5a6"><Icon name="luggage" /></span>
			<div>
				<strong>250+ bags and travel accessories reviewed</strong>
				<p>Each one stress-tested before it earned a recommendation.</p>
			</div>
		</li>
	</ol>

	<div class="sec-head">
		<span class="chip" style="--c1:#0b5f59;--c2:#1fb5a6"><Icon name="clipboard" /></span>
		<h2>What I know, and what I don’t</h2>
	</div>
	<p>
		“I know a lot about luggage” is a weak claim, so here is the specific list. These are the areas where I have
		hands-on experience:
	</p>
	<ul class="cards">
		<li>
			<span class="chip sm" style="--c1:#0a3d62;--c2:#2380c4"><Icon name="clipboard" size={18} /></span>
			<strong>Airline baggage policy</strong>
			Size and weight limits, fees, and how rules are applied at the counter and the gate.
		</li>
		<li>
			<span class="chip sm" style="--c1:#9a4a07;--c2:#f0a02a"><Icon name="archive" size={18} /></span>
			<strong>Carry-on optimization</strong>
			Fitting more into a bag that still goes in the overhead bin without a fight.
		</li>
		<li>
			<span class="chip sm" style="--c1:#0b5f59;--c2:#1fb5a6"><Icon name="gauge" size={18} /></span>
			<strong>What breaks, and when</strong>
			Wheel durability, zipper strength under weight, and how a bag looks after its fifth rough carousel.
		</li>
		<li>
			<span class="chip sm" style="--c1:#4a1d96;--c2:#8b5cf6"><Icon name="package" size={18} /></span>
			<strong>Packing strategy</strong>
			One-bag travel, packing systems, and the accessories that actually earn their space.
		</li>
	</ul>
	<div class="callout warm">
		<span class="chip sm"><Icon name="info" size={18} /></span>
		<div>
			<strong>Where my limits are.</strong> My experience is real-world, not laboratory testing. I don’t run bags
			through a lab rig. My airline background is strongest on luggage, carry-on and checked-bag rules. On topics
			further from it, such as handbags, outdoor gear or kids’ bags, I lean more on research and will say so in
			the article. And airline rules change, so check the carrier before you fly.
		</div>
	</div>

	<div class="sec-head">
		<span class="chip" style="--c1:#8a1546;--c2:#e5568a"><Icon name="search" /></span>
		<h2>The gap I kept seeing</h2>
	</div>
	<p>
		When I went looking for luggage advice, the same four problems kept turning up. They are the reason this site
		exists.
	</p>
	<ul class="cards">
		<li>
			<span class="chip sm" style="--c1:#8a1546;--c2:#e5568a"><Icon name="eye" size={18} /></span>
			<strong>Showroom verdicts</strong>
			Reviews written after a bag was unboxed, not after it was dragged through an airport.
		</li>
		<li>
			<span class="chip sm" style="--c1:#0a3d62;--c2:#2380c4"><Icon name="refreshcw" size={18} /></span>
			<strong>Stale baggage rules</strong>
			Fees and size limits copied from page to page long after the airline changed them.
		</li>
		<li>
			<span class="chip sm" style="--c1:#1b2447;--c2:#4c5fb0"><Icon name="users" size={18} /></span>
			<strong>No operations view</strong>
			Very little from someone who has actually handled bags and enforced airline policy.
		</li>
		<li>
			<span class="chip sm" style="--c1:#a53a0a;--c2:#f98a45"><Icon name="link" size={18} /></span>
			<strong>Advice in fragments</strong>
			Bag choice, fees and packing treated as separate questions, when you decide them together.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<div class="sec-head" id="how-i-test">
		<span class="chip" style="--c1:#0a3d62;--c2:#2380c4"><Icon name="route" /></span>
		<h2>How every bag gets tested</h2>
	</div>
	<p>
		My rule is simple: <strong>I review a bag only after real transit abuse.</strong> That means three places
		where luggage really gets punished.
	</p>
	<ol class="gauntlet">
		<li>
			<span class="chip sm" style="--c1:#9a4a07;--c2:#f0a02a"><Icon name="archive" size={18} /></span>
			<strong>Overhead bins</strong>
			Does it fit, squeeze and slide in as promised, flight after flight?
		</li>
		<li>
			<span class="chip sm" style="--c1:#8a1546;--c2:#e5568a"><Icon name="drop" size={18} /></span>
			<strong>Gate checks</strong>
			What happens when the flight is full and your carry-on gets tagged at the door.
		</li>
		<li>
			<span class="chip sm" style="--c1:#0b5f59;--c2:#1fb5a6"><Icon name="refresh" size={18} /></span>
			<strong>Baggage carousels</strong>
			Wheels, handles and zippers after the belt has had its turn.
		</li>
	</ol>
	<p>My promises to you:</p>
	<ul class="ticks">
		<li>I’ll tell you what I tested and what I only researched.</li>
		<li>I’ll say where a bag failed, not just where it shined.</li>
		<li>I’ll point you to the airline for the final word on fees and limits.</li>
		<li>I’ll keep affiliate links separate from my verdicts. <a href="/disclosure/">Here is exactly how.</a></li>
	</ul>

	<div class="sec-head">
		<span class="chip" style="--c1:#12482a;--c2:#47a05f"><Icon name="compass" /></span>
		<h2>What you’ll find here</h2>
	</div>
	<p>
		This site is for frequent flyers and vacation travelers choosing luggage and packing systems. Nine topics
		cover the whole trip, from the airline fee table to repairing a broken zipper. Topics with published guides
		link straight through.
	</p>
	<ul class="topics">
		{
			topicList.map((t) => (
				<li>
					<a class={`tcard${t.soon ? ' soon' : ''}`} href={t.href} style={t.style}>
						<span class="chip sm">
							<Icon name={t.icon} size={18} />
						</span>
						<span>
							<strong>{t.name}</strong>
							<small>{t.blurb}</small>
						</span>
					</a>
				</li>
			))
		}
	</ul>

	<section class="finish" aria-labelledby="finish-title">
		<h2 id="finish-title">Let’s get your bag home in one piece</h2>
		<p>
			Pack smarter, travel farther. That’s the whole idea, and I’d love to have you along. Start with a guide,
			and if something is unclear or wrong, tell me. I read what you send.
		</p>
		<div class="ab-hero-cta" style="margin-top:1.2rem">
			<a class="btn" href="/topic/airline-baggage-fees-and-carry-on-rules/">
				<Icon name="plane" size={18} /> Start with airline baggage fees
			</a>
			<a class="btn ghost" href="mailto:iverjcalloway@gmail.com?subject=Hello%20from%20Baggage%20Gear">
				<Icon name="mail" size={18} /> Email Iver
			</a>
		</div>
		<ul class="finish-links">
			<li><a href="/contact/">Contact page</a></li>
			<li><a href="/disclosure/">How this site earns money</a></li>
			<li><a href="https://www.facebook.com/IverCalloway/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Facebook</a></li>
		</ul>
		<p class="sign">Iver Calloway, Miami, Florida</p>
	</section>
</StaticPage>
